<DocsLayout title="Haft roadmap after v9" description="What works in the current release, what is deliberately outside it, and which gaps remain open without turning them into promises.">
  <h1>Roadmap</h1>

  <p>
    The current release is
    <a href="https://github.com/m0n0x41d/haft/releases/tag/v9.0.2" target="_blank" rel="noopener">v9.0.2</a>.
    This page separates shipped behavior from open work. An issue, branch,
    design, or experiment is not a product promise.
  </p>

  <h2>Available now</h2>

  <ul>
    <li>FPF concern search, exact lookup, and full source inspection;</li>
    <li>12 independent skills, including <code>h-reason</code> as the umbrella entry;</li>
    <li>local typed project memory written only for a concrete later use;</li>
    <li>code, decision, specification, invariant, and note orientation in one graph;</li>
    <li>project setup with automatic default memory and compatible upgrades;</li>
    <li>specification health, evidence freshness, and drift signals;</li>
    <li>CLI, skills, and MCP over one local project state;</li>
    <li>runner-neutral commission records for external integrations.</li>
  </ul>

  <h2>Deliberately outside v9</h2>

  <ul>
    <li>a standalone coding agent, TUI, or desktop wrapper;</li>
    <li><code>haft run</code>, <code>haft harness</code>, and bundled Open-Sleigh execution;</li>
    <li>a universal reasoning workflow or public <code>h-plan</code> stage;</li>
    <li>automatic patch application, merge, push, deploy, or publication;</li>
    <li>automatic merging or splitting of project identities;</li>
    <li>a claim that dense or hybrid retrieval outperforms simpler search.</li>
  </ul>

  <h2>Open product gaps</h2>

  <ul>
    <li><strong>Team runtime.</strong> Git review and partial import exist; complete authority-aware replay and safe shared multi-worktree identity do not.</li>
    <li><strong>Ceremony calibration.</strong> The hardest UX problem remains choosing enough structure for the cost of error without turning small work into bureaucracy.</li>
    <li><strong>Identity reconciliation.</strong> Public v9 identity changes are alias-only; reviewed merge and split need a separate contract.</li>
    <li><strong>Retrieval evaluation.</strong> Embedding compatibility exists, but superiority claims require a real parity measurement rather than intuition.</li>
  </ul>

  <p>
    These are directions and return conditions, not release commitments. Check
    the repository for work that has actually shipped.
  </p>

  <h2>Where to check current work</h2>

  <ul>
    <li><a href="https://github.com/m0n0x41d/haft/releases" target="_blank" rel="noopener">GitHub Releases</a> for published versions;</li>
    <li><a href="https://github.com/m0n0x41d/haft/blob/main/CHANGELOG.md" target="_blank" rel="noopener">CHANGELOG.md</a> for shipped changes;</li>
    <li><a href="https://github.com/m0n0x41d/haft/issues" target="_blank" rel="noopener">GitHub issues</a> for open discussion;</li>
    <li><code>haft version</code>, <code>haft doctor</code>, and <code>haft interface</code> for the installation you are using.</li>
  </ul>
</DocsLayout>
